        "answer": "IDEA grants parents the right to request an Independent Educational Evaluation (IEE) conducted by a qualified examiner outside the district. When parents disagree with the district's evaluation, the district must either fund the IEE at public expense or file for a due process hearing to defend the adequacy of its own evaluation. The district cannot simply refuse without taking one of those two actions.",
